---
title: Getting started
pageSlug: getting-started
mod: epicquest-hub
section: getting-started
order: 1
---

Hub only pastes on a **new world**. If you already created the world, changing coordinates will not move anything. Delete the world or start another.

1. Put a `.schem` or `.nbt` in `config/epicquest_hub/`.
2. Point `epicquest_hub-common.toml` at that file. Set paste and spawn.
3. Create a new world. The overworld is void. No dirt, no vanilla platform.
4. First start pastes the hub, sets world spawn, and remembers the bounds for protection.
5. Anyone who joins, or respawns in the overworld without a bed, lands on your spawn.

Works singleplayer and on a dedicated server. It will not paste a second time after a reload.

This is the lobby. Put [EpicQuest Dungeoning](/mods/epicquest-dungeoning) keystones in the schematic if the hub is where people pick a dungeon. Put a [BassSanctum](/mods/bass-sanctum) portal block if that dimension is a side room.
